From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The Deadmines' route lanterns go out when the server asks
 (patch 0096)

Rhahk'Zor's collapse (Basin Battle) brings the mine down section by section, and the lanterns
along its route should go out with them. Patch 0091 darkens lanterns only inside the aftermath
variant, which loads with patch 0087's marker, so none could go out one at a time.

New module deadmines_route_lamps: the server keeps one model-less game object of entry 500099
(just under 0087's marker, 500100) for each lantern it wants out, whose GUID's low 24 bits are the
lantern's place in the mine's WMO (MODD index). Like 0087's marker the state is derived from the
object snapshot (live, map 36), so a late join, a destroy, a reconnect or leaving the map need no
second protocol. Only the nine indices in ROUTE_LANTERNS (162, 184, 186, 199, 217, 414, 421, 422,
424) are honoured; any other GUID is ignored.

While a lantern is named, every world point light (the mine's own MOLT lights and the lights a
lantern's model carries, which spawn as the same WorldPointLight) within LANTERN_REACH (1.6 yd, as
0091) of its pivot goes to intensity 0, its strength kept in a PutOut component; when the marker
goes the strength comes back. The pivot is the model's MODD position through the mine placement's
world_from_local (the WmoPortalInstance whose handle names az_deadmines_b.wmo). While any lantern
is named, or a light is still out, it looks at every light each frame (the mine streams in after
its markers, a reload under the markers spawns full lights, the model and a light can land late);
a light that is out but no longer named is put back. Lights with a parent (a carried torch) are
never touched. Nothing is done unless the server sends a marker: an empty set with nothing out
returns at once.

The lantern's own model stays where it hangs; only its light goes (0091 found its glass glows
whatever is near). The ship still goes only with 0087's marker: hiding it without the reload is
not possible in a small patch (see Basin Battle's docs/deadmines-aftermath.md).

HasActionCombat() is 31: the server sends the markers only to this round. ROUTE_LANTERNS is
mirrored in Basin Battle's htl-map/src/deadmines/aftermath.rs.
---
diff --git a/crates/benilla-app/src/deadmines_route_lamps.rs b/crates/benilla-app/src/deadmines_route_lamps.rs
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..de3f90c7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/benilla-app/src/deadmines_route_lamps.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,299 @@
+//! Basin Battle's route lanterns, not a stock 1.12 behavior. While Rhahk'Zor brings the Deadmines
+//! down the server asks, one game object at a time, for the lanterns along his route to go out
+//! (patch 0096). Each is a model-less game object of entry [`MARKER_ENTRY`] whose GUID's low 24
+//! bits are the lantern's place in the mine's WMO (MODD index); it stands for as long as that
+//! lantern is out. Like patch 0087's marker the state is derived from the snapshot, so late joins,
+//! destroy packets, reconnects and leaving the map need no second protocol, and a client that
+//! never gets one does nothing.
+//!
+//! A lantern's own light is the mine's (MOLT) within [`LANTERN_REACH`] of its pivot, as patch 0091
+//! finds it: that light goes to intensity 0 and its authored strength is kept to put back. The
+//! lantern itself stays where it hangs. A mine reloaded under the markers (the aftermath marker)
+//! spawns its lights at full strength again, and they go out again the frame they appear.
+use std::collections::BTreeSet;
+
+use benilla_assets::coords::wow_to_bevy;
+use benilla_assets::WmoModel;
+use benilla_protocol::EntityKind;
+use benilla_world::lighting::WorldPointLight;
+use benilla_world::schedule::{WorldLive, WorldStage};
+use benilla_world::wmo_portal::WmoPortalInstance;
+use benilla_world::world_map::CurrentMap;
+use bevy::math::Affine3A;
+use bevy::prelude::*;
+
+use crate::net::{Guid, NetEntity, ObjectStore};
+
+/// The marker's entry, just under patch 0087's 500100 (500101 and up are the server's own pieces). Mirrored in Basin Battle's server.
+pub(crate) const MARKER_ENTRY: u32 = 500099;
+/// The lanterns a marker may name (MODD indices of the mine's WMO); any other is ignored.
+/// Mirrored in Basin Battle's htl-map/src/deadmines/aftermath.rs.
+pub(crate) const ROUTE_LANTERNS: &[u32] = &[162, 184, 186, 199, 217, 414, 421, 422, 424];
+/// A put-out lantern's own lights are the mine's within this of its pivot (yd), as patch 0091.
+const LANTERN_REACH: f32 = 1.6;
+
+/// The lanterns the server has put out, from the object snapshot.
+#[derive(Resource, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub(crate) struct RouteLamps(pub(crate) BTreeSet<u32>);
+
+/// A light put out: the strength it had.
+#[derive(Component)]
+struct PutOut(f32);
+
+pub(crate) fn plugin(app: &mut App) {
+    app.init_resource::<RouteLamps>().add_systems(
+        Update,
+        (sync, apply)
+            .chain()
+            .after(WorldStage::Input)
+            .before(WorldStage::Stream),
+    );
+}
+
+/// The lantern a marker's GUID names: `0xF110` (game object), the entry, then the lantern.
+fn lantern_of(guid: u64) -> Option<u32> {
+    let head = (0xF110_u64 << 24) | u64::from(MARKER_ENTRY);
+    let lantern = (guid & 0xFF_FFFF) as u32;
+    ((guid >> 24) == head && ROUTE_LANTERNS.contains(&lantern)).then_some(lantern)
+}
+
+fn sync(
+    live: Res<WorldLive>,
+    map: Option<Res<CurrentMap>>,
+    objects: Query<(&Guid, &NetEntity, &ObjectStore)>,
+    mut lamps: ResMut<RouteLamps>,
+) {
+    let out: BTreeSet<u32> = if live.0 && map.is_some_and(|m| m.0 == 36) {
+        objects
+            .iter()
+            .filter(|(_, net, fields)| {
+                net.kind == EntityKind::GameObject
+                    && net.display_id.unwrap_or(0) == 0
+                    && fields.0.object_entry() == Some(MARKER_ENTRY)
+            })
+            .filter_map(|(guid, _, _)| lantern_of(guid.0))
+            .collect()
+    } else {
+        BTreeSet::new()
+    };
+    if lamps.0 != out {
+        lamps.0 = out;
+    }
+}
+
+/// Whether a placement is the mine's own WMO (its handle's path names the root).
+fn is_mine(handle: &Handle<WmoModel>) -> bool {
+    handle.path().is_some_and(|p| {
+        p.path()
+            .to_string_lossy()
+            .to_ascii_lowercase()
+            .contains("az_deadmines_b.wmo")
+    })
+}
+
+/// Where each named lantern hangs in the world, for a mine placed by `world_from_local`. A
+/// doodad the model does not have yields nothing.
+fn spots_in(out: &BTreeSet<u32>, model: &WmoModel, world_from_local: Affine3A) -> Vec<Vec3> {
+    out.iter()
+        .filter_map(|&index| model.doodads.get(index as usize))
+        .map(|d| world_from_local.transform_point3(wow_to_bevy(d.position)))
+        .collect()
+}
+
+/// Where each named lantern hangs, in the mines placed in `instances`. A mine whose model has
+/// not landed yields nothing.
+fn spots(
+    out: &BTreeSet<u32>,
+    instances: &Query<&WmoPortalInstance>,
+    models: &Assets<WmoModel>,
+) -> Vec<Vec3> {
+    instances
+        .iter()
+        .filter(|i| is_mine(&i.handle))
+        .filter_map(|i| Some(spots_in(out, models.get(&i.handle)?, i.world_from_local)))
+        .flatten()
+        .collect()
+}
+
+/// What a light by `at` does under `spots`: the strength to keep when it is put out, or to put
+/// back when it no longer is. `put` is the strength it was put out from.
+#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]
+enum Settle {
+    Keep,
+    PutOut(f32),
+    PutBack(f32),
+}
+
+fn settle(spots: &[Vec3], at: Vec3, intensity: f32, put: Option<f32>) -> Settle {
+    let reach = LANTERN_REACH * LANTERN_REACH;
+    let dark = spots.iter().any(|s| s.distance_squared(at) < reach);
+    match (dark, put) {
+        (true, None) => Settle::PutOut(intensity),
+        (false, Some(was)) => Settle::PutBack(was),
+        _ => Settle::Keep,
+    }
+}
+
+/// Put out the lights of the named lanterns, and put back those no longer named. While any
+/// lantern is named (or a light is still out) it looks at every light each frame, which a mine
+/// streaming in after its markers, a reload under them, a late model and a late light all need;
+/// with none named and none out it returns at once.
+fn apply(
+    mut commands: Commands,
+    lamps: Res<RouteLamps>,
+    models: Res<Assets<WmoModel>>,
+    instances: Query<&WmoPortalInstance>,
+    mut lights: Query<
+        (Entity, &Transform, &mut WorldPointLight, Option<&PutOut>),
+        Without<ChildOf>,
+    >,
+    mut active: Local<bool>,
+) {
+    if lamps.0.is_empty() && !*active {
+        return;
+    }
+    let spots = spots(&lamps.0, &instances, &models);
+    let mut any_out = false;
+    for (entity, at, mut light, put) in &mut lights {
+        match settle(&spots, at.translation, light.intensity, put.map(|p| p.0)) {
+            Settle::PutOut(was) => {
+                commands.entity(entity).insert(PutOut(was));
+                light.intensity = 0.0;
+                any_out = true;
+            }
+            Settle::PutBack(was) => {
+                light.intensity = was;
+                commands.entity(entity).remove::<PutOut>();
+            }
+            Settle::Keep => any_out |= put.is_some(),
+        }
+    }
+    *active = any_out;
+}
+
+#[cfg(test)]
+mod tests {
+    use super::*;
+    use benilla_protocol::ObjectFields;
+
+    fn marker(lantern: u32) -> u64 {
+        (0xF110_u64 << 48) | (u64::from(MARKER_ENTRY) << 24) | u64::from(lantern)
+    }
+
+    fn spawn_marker(app: &mut App, guid: u64, entry: u32) -> Entity {
+        app.world_mut()
+            .spawn((
+                Guid(guid),
+                NetEntity {
+                    kind: EntityKind::GameObject,
+                    display_id: Some(0),
+                    scale: 1.0,
+                },
+                ObjectStore(ObjectFields::from_pairs(&[(3, entry)])),
+            ))
+            .id()
+    }
+
+    fn app() -> App {
+        let mut app = App::new();
+        app.insert_resource(WorldLive(true))
+            .insert_resource(CurrentMap(36))
+            .init_resource::<Assets<WmoModel>>();
+        plugin(&mut app);
+        app
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn a_marker_names_its_lantern_and_only_a_route_lantern() {
+        assert_eq!(lantern_of(marker(414)), Some(414));
+        assert_eq!(lantern_of(marker(162)), Some(162));
+        assert_eq!(lantern_of(marker(415)), None, "not on the route");
+        assert_eq!(lantern_of(0xF110_07A1_84FF_FFFF), None, "patch 0087's marker is not a lantern");
+        assert_eq!(lantern_of((0xF110_u64 << 48) | (500098u64 << 24) | 414), None);
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn the_snapshot_names_the_lanterns_out_and_a_map_exit_or_a_destroy_clears_them() {
+        let mut app = app();
+        let a = spawn_marker(&mut app, marker(414), MARKER_ENTRY);
+        spawn_marker(&mut app, marker(421), MARKER_ENTRY);
+        spawn_marker(&mut app, marker(415), MARKER_ENTRY);
+        spawn_marker(&mut app, marker(422), 500100);
+        app.update();
+        assert_eq!(
+            app.world().resource::<RouteLamps>().0,
+            BTreeSet::from([414, 421])
+        );
+        app.world_mut().despawn(a);
+        app.update();
+        assert_eq!(app.world().resource::<RouteLamps>().0, BTreeSet::from([421]));
+        app.world_mut().resource_mut::<CurrentMap>().0 = 0;
+        app.update();
+        assert!(app.world().resource::<RouteLamps>().0.is_empty());
+    }
+
+    fn doodad(position: [f32; 3]) -> benilla_formats::WmoDoodad {
+        benilla_formats::WmoDoodad {
+            model: "lantern.m2".into(),
+            position,
+            orientation: [0., 0., 0., 1.],
+            scale: 1.,
+            color: [255; 4],
+        }
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn with_no_mine_placed_a_marker_touches_no_light_and_with_none_the_system_idles() {
+        let mut app = app();
+        let light = app
+            .world_mut()
+            .spawn((
+                WorldPointLight {
+                    color: [1.0, 0.8, 0.5],
+                    intensity: 12.0,
+                    range: 48.0,
+                },
+                Transform::from_translation(Vec3::new(1.0, 2.0, 3.0)),
+            ))
+            .id();
+        app.update();
+        app.update();
+        assert_eq!(app.world().get::<WorldPointLight>(light).unwrap().intensity, 12.0);
+        let marker = spawn_marker(&mut app, marker(414), MARKER_ENTRY);
+        app.update();
+        app.update();
+        assert!(app.world().resource::<RouteLamps>().0.contains(&414));
+        assert_eq!(
+            app.world().get::<WorldPointLight>(light).unwrap().intensity,
+            12.0,
+            "no mine placed: nothing to find the lantern in"
+        );
+        assert!(app.world().get::<PutOut>(light).is_none());
+        app.world_mut().despawn(marker);
+        app.update();
+        assert_eq!(app.world().get::<WorldPointLight>(light).unwrap().intensity, 12.0);
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn a_named_lantern_hangs_where_the_placement_puts_its_pivot() {
+        let mut model = WmoModel::default();
+        model.doodads = (0..430).map(|i| doodad([i as f32, 0.0, 0.0])).collect();
+        let at = Affine3A::from_translation(Vec3::new(100.0, 200.0, 300.0));
+        let spots = spots_in(&BTreeSet::from([414, 9999]), &model, at);
+        assert_eq!(spots, vec![at.transform_point3(wow_to_bevy([414.0, 0.0, 0.0]))]);
+        assert!(spots_in(&BTreeSet::new(), &model, at).is_empty());
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn a_light_by_a_named_lantern_goes_out_and_comes_back_when_it_is_put_back() {
+        let lamp = Vec3::new(5.0, 2.0, -3.0);
+        let near = lamp + Vec3::new(0.0, 0.4, 0.0);
+        let far = lamp + Vec3::new(9.0, 0.0, 0.0);
+        let spots = [lamp];
+        assert_eq!(settle(&spots, near, 12.0, None), Settle::PutOut(12.0));
+        assert_eq!(settle(&spots, near, 0.0, Some(12.0)), Settle::Keep, "already out");
+        assert_eq!(settle(&spots, far, 12.0, None), Settle::Keep, "another lantern's light");
+        assert_eq!(settle(&[], near, 0.0, Some(12.0)), Settle::PutBack(12.0));
+        assert_eq!(settle(&[], near, 12.0, None), Settle::Keep, "nothing named: nothing done");
+    }
+}
